.TH CITIES-FROM-SPACE 1 "August 2026" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cities-from-space \- generate procedural city decals for planet models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cities-from-space
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-size\fR \fIPIXELS\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-num\fR \fICOUNT\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cities-from-space
is a procedural texture generation program designed to create city decals for space games. These decals are intended to be pasted onto spherical planet models to represent sprawling urban areas.
.PP
The program outputs two PNG images: a diffuse map for the daylight side of the planet, and an emittance (emission) map featuring a bloom effect to represent glowing city lights on the night side of the planet.
.PP
The city structures are generated using a recursive circle algorithm to build a natural-looking metropolitan footprint. The program then overlays a network of grid roads, main arteries (using midpoint displacement), and loop roads, seamlessly blending them using an alpha-mask blur.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-size\fR \fIPIXELS\fR
Set the width and height of a single city image in pixels. The generated images are always square. The default size is 512.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-num\fR \fICOUNT\fR
Specify the number of individual cities to generate. If greater than 1, the program will combine the resulting cities into a single texture atlas. The dimensions of the atlas are automatically calculated to be as close to a square grid as possible. The default count is 1.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print a brief usage message and exit.
.SH REQUIRED FILES
The program requires the following source texture PNG files to be present in the working directory before execution:
.TP
.B city-texture.png
Used as the base texture for the urban areas.
.TP
.B road-texture.png
Used to color the diffuse map road networks.
.TP
.B lights-texture.png
Used to map colors to the nighttime emittance map.
.SH OUTPUT FILES
The program writes two files to the current working directory, overwriting any existing files with the same names:
.TP
.B diffuse_map.png
The final composited diffuse texture atlas (daytime).
.TP
.B emittance_map.png
The final composited emittance texture atlas with bloom effects (nighttime).
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a single 1024x1024 city decal:
.PP
.RS
.B cities-from-space \-s 1024
.RE
.PP
Generate an atlas of 16 cities, with each city being 256x256 pixels. This will result in 1024x1024 output atlas images (a 4x4 grid):
.PP
.RS
.B cities-from-space \-\-size 256 \-\-num 16
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, and 1 if there is an error (such as missing texture files or invalid command-line arguments).

